course: dictionary
lesson: 11158
title: Winch: a machine that lifts and pulls
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A winch is a machine with a rope or chain wound round a turning drum. When you turn its big handle, the drum turns, and the rope pulls a heavy load up or along. «Knights so heavy they were winched onto their horses by crane» tells you that the knights were too heavy to climb up by themselves, so something lifted them.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. Heavy things need help to move. Crane is a big machine that lifts. Put them together and winched must mean lifted or pulled with a machine. Then test it: «The knights were lifted onto their horses by crane» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Winch can also be a verb. To winch something means to lift or pull it with a winch. In the news, «rescue helicopters winch people to safety», so the word shows a machine doing the hard work of moving someone.
fact: A winch is a machine with a rope or chain wound round a drum.
fact: To winch means to lift or pull something with a winch.
fact: A winch makes it easier to lift a heavy load by turning a big handle.
fact: «Wells once used a winch to raise buckets of water.»
fact: «Winch» can be a noun (a winch) or a verb (to winch).
exercise: «The knights were so heavy they were winched onto their horses by crane.» What does winched mean? | Hidden inside a castle | Painted in bright colours | *Lifted or pulled up with a machine | Dropped quickly to the ground
exercise: «Rescue helicopters winch people to safety.» What does winch mean in this sentence? | To sing a sad song | *To lift or pull using a machine with a rope | To hide from the sea | To shout loudly to a crowd
exercise: «Wells once used a winch to raise buckets of water.» Find and copy one word that means lift up. | water | *raise | wells | buckets
test: Which clue helps you work out the meaning of winched in «knights so heavy they were winched onto their horses by crane»? | The word filthy | *The words heavy and crane | The word flat | The word wild
test: In a winch, turning a big handle does what? | Makes the load lighter in colour | Makes the rope disappear | *Makes it easier to lift a heavy load | Stops the rope from moving
exam: «Tow trucks winch cars out of ditches.» What is the most likely meaning of winch here? | *Pull the car out using a machine | Park the car in a garage | Paint the car | Sell the car
